<header class="page-intro about-intro"><span class="eyebrow">HELLO, I’M LAKSHMIKANT</span><h1>An engineer by trade.<br><em>A builder by instinct.</em></h1></header>
<div class="about-body"><aside class="about-card"><div class="large-monogram" aria-hidden="true">ld<span>.</span></div><div class="about-location"><span class="status-dot"></span> Bengaluru, India</div><p>Optimist. Dreamer.<br>Learner. Programmer.<br>Supergeek.</p><a class="text-link" href="{{ site.linkedin }}">Find me on LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></aside><div class="prose"><p class="lead-paragraph">I like turning ideas into working software. Sometimes that means a distributed system. Sometimes it means an app that saves someone a few taps.</p><p>I’m a software engineer at PayPal in Bengaluru, where I work on payments and backend systems. Over the past decade, my work has taken me through APIs, data pipelines, distributed services, and the details that make systems dependable.</p><p>Before PayPal, I built software at AppZen, Clairvoyant, and Persistent Systems. That experience shaped how I approach problems: understand the moving pieces, keep the design clear, and care about what happens after something ships.</p><h2>Curiosity, with an output.</h2><p>Outside that work, I build <a href="/work/">small apps and tools</a>. Minku Learns explores early learning. Clean My Links makes sharing a little tidier. Unknown Messenger removes an extra step before a conversation.</p><p>I’m also curious about AI as a practical part of making software: research tools, codebase documentation, and experiments that turn an idea into something testable. AutoLLD is one example.</p><h2>What you’ll find here</h2><p>This is a home for things I’ve made and ideas I’m working through. The projects are here already; the <a href="/writing/">notebook</a> will grow as I write.</p><p>If something here resonates, or you’re building something interesting, <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">say hello</a>.</p></div></div>
